                    <characteristic name="Type" typeId="13f9-a26b-05af-3459">Infantry (Special Character, Chaos Dwarf)</characteristic>
                  </characteristics>
                </profile>
              </profiles>
              <rules>
                <rule name="The Granite Guard" id="c2a1-2091-bffd-39bc" hidden="false">
                  <description>If Astragoth Ironhand is included in your army, you may upgrade one unit of Razers to the Granite Guard for a cost of +2 points per model. This unit always counts as fighting behind a defended obstacle in the first round of close combat, and do not suffer -1 To Hit when choosing Stand &amp; Shoot as a charge reaction. The unit must be equipped with blunderbusses.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Mechanical Body" id="3190-f66b-e5e8-a7f3" hidden="false">
                  <description>Astragoth may never march or charge longer than his Movement value. He will still pursue and flee at a normal speed.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Overdrive" id="a770-b83b-1164-cb57" hidden="false">
                  <description>If Astragoth successfully Hits with 3 or more Attacks in Close Combat, he can immediately make an additional 3 Attacks. These attacks may not generate any further additional attacks.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
              <selectionEntryGroups>
